    "story_hero": {
      "type": "hlt-hero",
      "settings": {
        "layout": "split",
        "media_side": "right",
        "background": "cream",
        "ratio_mobile": "1 / 1",
        "ratio": "4 / 3",
        "hide_empty_media": false,
        "overlay": 0,
        "mobile_text_position": "center",
        "parallax_speed": "0.12",
        "show_sparkles": false,
        "overline": "Our story",
        "quote": "",
        "quote_attribution": "",
        "heading": "We kept the noodle and changed what's in it.",
        "use_h1": true,
        "subheading": "",
        "body": "<p>Noodles and rice are how most of us eat in Singapore. We would rather change what the noodle is made of than ask you to give it up.</p><p>W0W® is made in Singapore by KosmodeHealth, which began as a spin-off from the Food Science and Technology department at the National University of Singapore.</p>",
        "body_color": "default",
        "button_label": "See ProTEGO®",
        "button_scroll": false,
        "scroll_target": "#hlt-buy-box-packs",
        "button_link": "shopify://products/10-individual-pack-80g-w0w®-protego™",
        "button_style": "link",
        "wave_bottom": false,
        "wave_color": "paper",
        "padding_top": 72,
        "padding_bottom": 72
      }
    },
    "story_why": {
      "type": "hlt-media-text",
      "blocks": {
        "overline": {
          "type": "overline",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Why we started"
          }
        },
        "heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Grow it once, use it twice.",
            "size": "hlt-h2"
          }
        },
        "body_second_life": {
          "type": "body",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Pressing peanuts for oil leaves solids behind, called oil meal. Making potato noodles leaves sweet potato fibre. Both are food that has already been grown and harvested once. We take the protein from the oil meal and the fibre from the sweet potato, and give them a second life in a noodle.</p>",
            "large": false
          }
        },
        "body_belief": {
          "type": "body",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We don't believe feeding people well means growing more. Using each crop twice is our part of the answer. We call it <strong>#Wastes2Health</strong>.</p>",
            "large": false
          }
        },
        "body_health": {
          "type": "body",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Your health still comes first. We only use a second-life ingredient where it is good for the person eating it. That is why two of ProTEGO®'s four ingredients are second-life: the peanut protein and the sweet potato fibre.</p>",
            "large": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "overline",
        "heading",
        "body_second_life",
        "body_belief",
        "body_health"
      ],
